  "cut_point": "To solve this problem, we need to carefully analyze the conditions provided:\n\n---\n\n### **Given:**\n\n- The person says: *If you add all the six two-digit numbers that can be made from the digits of the ticket number, half of the resulting sum will be exactly my ticket number.*\n\nLet:\n\n- The ticket number be **N**.\n- The digits of **N** be **a**, **b**, **c**, **d**, **e**, **f** (i.e., the number is a 6-digit number).",
  "reflection": {
    "verified_state": [
      "Let N denote the ticket number.",
      "The quoted condition states that half the sum of the six two-digit numbers formed from the digits of N equals N."
    ],
    "error_step": "- The digits of **N** be **a**, **b**, **c**, **d**, **e**, **f** (i.e., the number is a 6-digit number).",
    "error_reason": "This incorrectly assumes the ticket number has six digits. The phrase 'six two-digit numbers' indicates the ticket number has three digits, since three distinct digits produce 3×2 = 6 ordered two-digit numbers.",
    "new_direction": "Let N be a 3-digit number with digits a, b, c and sum the six ordered two-digit numbers formed from those digits, then set half that sum equal to N."
  }
